k"]]},{"id":"time","title":"Time","items":[["day","dzień","jen"],["night","noc","nots"],["morning","rano","RAH-noh"],["afternoon","popołudnie","poh-poh-WOOD-nyeh"],["week","tydzień","TIH-jen"],["month","miesiąc","MYEH-shonts"],["year","rok","rok"],["Monday","poniedziałek","poh-nyeh-JAH-wek"],["Tuesday","wtorek","FTOH-rek"],["Wednesday","środa","SHROH-dah"],["Thursday","czwartek","CHFAHR-tek"],["Friday","piątek","PYON-tek"],["Saturday","sobota","soh-BOH-tah"],["Sunday","niedziela","nyeh-JEH-lah"],["January","styczeń","STIH-chen"],["summer","lato","LAH-toh"],["winter","zima","ZHEE-mah"]]},{"id":"weather-and-nature","title":"Weather and nature","items":[["sun","słońce","SWOHN-tseh"],["rain","deszcz","deshch"],["snow","śnieg","shnyek"],["wind","wiatr","vyahtr"],["cloud","chmura","HMOO-rah"],["hot","gorąco","goh-RON-tsoh"],["cold","zimno","ZHEEM-noh"],["sea","morze","MOH-zheh"],["river","rzeka","ZHEH-kah"],["mountain","góra","GOO-rah"],["tree","drzewo","DZHEH-voh"],["flower","kwiat","kfyaht"],["sky","niebo","NYEH-boh"]]},{"id":"work-and-school","title":"Work and school","items":[["teacher","nauczyciel","nah-oo-CHIH-chel"],["student","student","STOO-dent"],["book","książka","KSHONSH-kah"],["pen","długopis","dwoo-GOH-pees"],["pencil","ołówek","oh-WOO-vek"],["paper","papier","PAH-pyer"],["computer","komputer","kom-POO-ter"],["phone","telefon","teh-LEH-fon"],["work","praca","PRAH-tsah"],["office","biuro","BYOO-roh"],["doctor","lekarz","LEH-kahsh"],["police officer","policjant","poh-LEE-tsyahnt"],["lesson","lekcja","LEK-tsyah"],["exam","egzamin","eg-ZAH-meen"]]},{"id":"describing","title":"Describing","items":[["big","duży","DOO-zhih"],["small","mały","MAH-wih"],["good","dobry","DOH-brih"],["bad","zły","zwih"],["new","nowy","NOH-vih"],["old","stary","STAH-rih"],["beautiful","piękny","PYENK-nih"],["ugly","brzydki","BZHID-kee"],["fast","szybki","SHIP-kee"],["slow","wolny","VOHL-nih"],["easy","łatwy","WAHT-fih"],["difficult","trudny","TROOD-nih"],["cheap","tani","TAH-nee"],["expensive","drogi","DROH-gee"],["clean","czysty","CHIH-stih"],["dirty","brudny","BROOD-nih"]]},{"id":"common-verbs","title":"Common verbs","items":[["to be","być","bihch"],["to have","mieć","myech"],["to go (on foot)","iść","eeshch"],["to want","chcieć","htsyech"],["to eat","jeść","yeshch"],["to drink","pić","peech"],["to speak","mówić","MOO-veech"],["to see","widzieć","VEE-jech"],["to come","przychodzić","pshih-HOH-jeech"],["to give","dawać","DAH-vahch"],["to know","wiedzieć","VYEH-jech"],["to do / make","robić","ROH-beech"],["to say","mówić","MOO-veech"],["to like","lubić","LOO-beech"],["to live","mieszkać","MYESH-kahch"],["to work","pracować","prah-TSOH-vahch"],["to buy","kupować","koo-POH-vahch"],["to read","czytać","CHIH-tahch"],["to write","pisać","PEE-sahch"],["to sleep","spać","spahch"],["to learn","uczyć się","OO-chihch sheh"],["to help","pomagać","poh-MAH-gahch"],["to need","potrzebować","poh-tsheh-BOH-vahch"],["to love","kochać","KOH-hahch"]]}],"grammar":[{"id":"pronouns","title":"Pronouns","text":["Polish often drops the subject, because the verb ending shows who is speaking. Pan / Pani are the formal \"you\"."],"rows":[["I","ja","yah"],["you (informal)","ty","tih"],["he / she / it","on / ona / ono","on / OH-nah / OH-noh"],["we","my","mih"],["you all","wy","vih"],["they","oni / one","OH-nee / OH-neh"],["you (formal, m / f)","Pan / Pani","pahn / PAH-nee"]],"ex":[["I am a student","ja jestem studentem","yah YES-tem stoo-DEN-tem"],["you are tall","ty jesteś wysoki","tih YES-tesh vih-SOH-kee"],["she is my sister","ona jest moją siostrą","OH-nah yest MOH-yon SHOS-tron"],["we are friends","my jesteśmy przyjaciółmi","mih yes-TESH-mih pshih-yah-CHOOW-mee"],["they are teachers","oni są nauczycielami","OH-nee son nah-oo-chih-cheh-LAH-mee"]]},{"id":"singular-and-plural","title":"Singular and plural","text":["Masculine: add -y or -i (or -e). Feminine: -a → -y or -i. Neuter: -o → -a. Some are irregular, so learn the plural with the word."],"rows":[["masculine","dom → domy","DOH-mih"],["masculine (soft)","kot → koty","KOH-tih"],["feminine","książka → książki","KSHONSH-kee"],["neuter","okno → okna","OK-nah"],["person (masculine)","student → studenci","stoo-DEN-chee"]],"ex":[["one house, houses","dom, domy","dom DOH-mih"],["one book, books","książka, książki","KSHONSH-kah KSHONSH-kee"],["one window, windows","okno, okna","OK-noh OK-nah"],["one cat, cats","kot, koty","kot KOH-tih"],["one student, students","student, studenci","STOO-dent stoo-DEN-chee"]]},{"id":"by-to-be","title":"Być: to be","text":[],"rows":[["I am","jestem","YES-tem"],["you are","jesteś","YES-tesh"],["he / she is","jest","yest"],["we are","jesteśmy","yes-TESH-mih"],["you all are","jesteście","yes-TESH-cheh"],["they are","są","son"]],"ex":[["I am English","jestem Anglikiem","YES-tem ahn-GLEE-kyem"],["he is a doctor","on jest lekarzem","on yest leh-KAH-zhem"],["we are tired","jesteśmy zmęczeni","yes-TESH-mih zmen-CHEH-nee"],["are you from Warsaw?","jesteś z Warszawy?","YES-tesh z vahr-SHAH-vih"],["they are at home","są w domu","son v DOH-moo"]]},{"id":"mie-to-have","title":"Mieć: to have","text":[],"rows":[["I have","mam","mahm"],["you have","masz","mahsh"],["he / she has","ma","mah"],["we have","mamy","MAH-mih"],["you all have","macie","MAH-cheh"],["they have","mają","MAH-yon"]],"ex":[["I have a brother","mam brata","mahm BRAH-tah"],["she has two cats","ona ma dwa koty","OH-nah mah dvah KOH-tih"],["we have time","mamy czas","MAH-mih chahs"],["do you have a pen?","masz długopis?","mahsh dwoo-GOH-pees"],["they have a car","mają samochód","MAH-yon sah-MOH-hoot"]]},{"id":"regular-verbs-present-tense","title":"Regular verbs (present tense)","text":["Many verbs end in -ać or -ić. Pracować (to work):"],"rows":[["ja","pracuję","prah-TSOO-yeh"],["ty","pracujesz","prah-TSOO-yesh"],["on / ona","pracuje","prah-TSOO-yeh"],["my","pracujemy","prah-tsoo-YEH-mih"],["wy","pracujecie","prah-tsoo-YEH-cheh"],["oni","pracują","prah-TSOO-yon"]],"ex":[["I work in a bank","pracuję w banku","prah-TSOO-yeh v BAHN-koo"],["you live in Warsaw","mieszkasz w Warszawie","MYESH-kahsh v vahr-SHAH-vyeh"],["she reads a book","ona czyta książkę","OH-nah CHIH-tah KSHONSH-keh"],["we learn Polish","uczymy się polskiego","oo-CHIH-mih sheh pol-SKYEH-goh"],["they buy bread","kupują chleb","koo-POO-yon hlep"]]},{"id":"i-to-go","title":"Iść: to go","text":["To go by transport use jechać (jadę, jedziesz...). Iść is on foot."],"rows":[["I go","idę","EE-deh"],["you go","idziesz","EE-jesh"],["he / she goes","idzie","EE-jeh"],["we go","idziemy","ee-JEH-mih"],["they go","idą","EE-don"]],"ex":[["I am going to school","idę do szkoły","EE-deh doh SHKOH-wih"],["where are you going?","dokąd idziesz?","DOH-kont EE-jesh"],["we are going home","idziemy do domu","ee-JEH-mih doh DOH-moo"],["she is going shopping","idzie na zakupy","EE-jeh nah zah-KOO-pih"],["let's go!","chodźmy!","HOJ-mih"]]},{"id":"basic-sentences","title":"Basic sentences","text":["Order is flexible, but the usual order is subject, verb, object. Adjectives come before the noun and agree in gender and number."],"rows":[["subject + verb + object","Jem chleb.","yem hlep"],["adjective before noun","duży dom","DOO-zhih dom"],["add time or place","Pracuję tu dzisiaj.","prah-TSOO-yeh too JEE-shay"]],"ex":[["I eat bread","jem chleb","yem hlep"],["Anna reads a book","Anna czyta książkę","AHN-nah CHIH-tah KSHONSH-keh"],["we live in a big house","mieszkamy w dużym domu","myesh-KAH-mih v DOO-zhim DOH-moo"],["he works here today","on dzisiaj tu pracuje","on JEE-shay too prah-TSOO-yeh"],["the dog is black","pies jest czarny","pyes yest CHAR-nih"]]},{"id":"negation","title":"Negation","text":["Put nie before the verb. Double negatives are normal: nic nie mam."],"rows":[["not","nie + verb","nyeh"],["nothing","nic","neets"],["nobody","nikt","neekt"],["never","nigdy","NEEG-dih"]],"ex":[["I do not speak French","nie mówię po francusku","nyeh MOO-vyeh poh frahn-TSOO-skoo"],["she does not live here","ona tu nie mieszka","OH-nah too nyeh MYESH-kah"],["I do not want anything","nic nie chcę","neets nyeh htseh"],["nobody is here","nikogo tu nie ma","nee-KOH-goh too nyeh mah"],["I never eat meat","nigdy nie jem mięsa","NEEG-dih nyeh yem MYEN-sah"]]},{"id":"asking-questions","title":"Asking questions","text":["Yes or no question: start with czy, or just raise your voice."],"rows":[["statement","Mówisz po angielsku.","MOO-veesh poh ahn-GYEL-skoo"],["question with czy","Czy mówisz po angielsku?","chih MOO-veesh poh ahn-GYEL-skoo"],["rising voice","Mówisz po angielsku?","MOO-veesh poh ahn-GYEL-skoo"]],"ex":[["do you speak English?","czy mówisz po angielsku?","chih MOO-veesh poh ahn-GYEL-skoo"],["is she a doctor?","czy ona jest lekarzem?","chih OH-nah yest leh-KAH-zhem"],["do you have a pen?","czy masz długopis?","chih mahsh dwoo-GOH-pees"],["are you tired?","czy jesteś zmęczony?","chih YES-tesh zmen-CHOH-nih"],["is it far?","czy to daleko?","chih toh dah-LEH-koh"]]},{"id":"question-words","title":"Question words","text":[],"rows":[["what","co","tsoh"],["who","kto","ktoh"],["where","gdzie","gjeh"],["when","kiedy","KYEH-dih"],["why","dlaczego","dlah-CHEH-goh"],["how","jak","yahk"],["which","który","KTOO-rih"],["how much / how many","ile","EE-leh"]],"ex":[["what is this?","co to jest?","tsoh toh yest"],["who is she?","kim ona jest?","keem OH-nah yest"],["where do you live?","gdzie mieszkasz?","gjeh MYESH-kahsh"],["when is the exam?","kiedy jest egzamin?","KYEH-dih yest eg-ZAH-meen"],["why are you late?","dlaczego jesteś spóźniony?","dlah-CHEH-goh YES-tesh spooz-NYOH-nih"],["how much is it?","ile to kosztuje?","EE-leh toh kosh-TOO-yeh"]]},{"id":"possessives","title":"Possessives","text":[],"rows":[["my","mój / moja / moje","mooy / MOH-yah / MOH-yeh"],["your (informal)","twój / twoja / twoje","tfooy / TFOH-yah / TFOH-yeh"],["his / her","jego / jej","YEH-goh / yay"],["our","nasz / nasza / nasze","nahsh / NAH-shah / NAH-sheh"],["your (plural)","wasz / wasza / wasze","vahsh / VAH-shah / VAH-sheh"],["their","ich","eeh"]],"ex":[["my house","mój dom","mooy dom"],["your friends","twoi przyjaciele","TFOH-ee pshih-yah-CHEH-leh"],["his sister","jego siostra","YEH-goh SHOS-trah"],["our teacher","nasz nauczyciel","nahsh nah-oo-CHIH-chel"],["my mother","moja matka","MOH-yah MAHT-kah"]]},{"id":"formal-vs-informal","title":"Formal vs informal","text":["ty / twój for friends. Pan / Pani for strangers, with the verb in the 3rd person (he / she form). Add \"Pan\" or \"Pani\" + name or title."],"rows":[["you, informal","ty","tih"],["you, formal (m)","Pan","pahn"],["you, formal (f)","Pani","PAH-nee"],["Mr","Pan + surname","pahn"],["Mrs / Ms","Pani + surname","PAH-nee"]],"ex":[["you speak (informal)","ty mówisz","tih MOO-veesh"],["you speak (formal, to a man)","Pan mówi","pahn MOO-vee"],["how are you? (informal)","jak się masz?","yahk sheh mahsh"],["how are you? (formal, to a woman)","jak się Pani ma?","yahk sheh PAH-nee mah"],["thank you, Mr Nowak","dziękuję, Panie Nowak","jen-KOO-yeh PAH-nyeh NOH-vahk"]]},{"id":"past-and-future-simple","title":"Past and future (simple)","text":["Past: verb stem + -ł + person ending (masculine) or -ła (feminine). Future: będę + infinitive."],"rows":[["I worked (m)","pracowałem","prah-tsoh-VAH-wem"],["I worked (f)","pracowałam","prah-tsoh-VAH-wahm"],["you worked (m)","pracowałeś","prah-tsoh-VAH-wesh"],["I will work","będę pracować","BEN-deh prah-TSOH-vahch"]],"ex":[["yesterday I worked (m)","wczoraj pracowałem","FCHOH-ray prah-tsoh-VAH-wem"],["she bought a book","kupiła książkę","koo-PEE-wah KSHONSH-keh"],["I went home (m)","poszedłem do domu","poh-SHED-wem doh DOH-moo"],["I will call you tomorrow","zadzwonię jutro","zahd-ZVOH-nyeh YOO-troh"],["we will eat at eight","zjemy o ósmej","ZYEH-mih oh OOS-may"]]}],"name":"Polish","id":"pl","badge":"Solid","note":"Starter speaking. Capitals mark the stressed syllable (almost always the second-last)."}